==Cultural impact==
[[File:WrestleMania 32 2016-04-03 19-00-16 ILCE-6000 9149 DxO (27799109971).jpg|thumb|upright|[[The New Day (professional wrestling)|The New Day]] dressed in Saiyan armor costumes]]
===Fandom===
Several celebrities and professional athletes from around the world have made references to characters from the ''Dragon Ball'' series.<ref name="cleveland">{{cite news |title=Celebs, athletes give 'Dragon Ball' pop culture super status |url=https://www.cleveland.com/entertainment/2019/01/celebs-athletes-give-dragon-ball-pop-culture-super-status.html |work=[[The Plain Dealer]] |date=January 15, 2019 |access-date=January 18, 2019 |archive-date=September 3, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200903173435/https://www.cleveland.com/entertainment/2019/01/celebs-athletes-give-dragon-ball-pop-culture-super-status.html |url-status=live }}</ref> For example, American UFC fighter [[Marcus Brimage]] cited the ''Dragon Ball Z'' series as one of his inspirations for taking up mixed-martial arts.<ref>[https://bleacherreport.com/articles/964872-marcus-brimage-credits-dbz-for-his-mma-career MMA: Marcus Brimage Credits Dragon Ball Z for His Career Choice]. Bleacher Report (2011-12-01). Retrieved on 2013-06-28.</ref> [[The New Day (professional wrestling)|The New Day]] appeared in [[Cosplay|full costumes patterned after Saiyan armor]] at [[WWE]]'s [[WrestleMania 32]] as a part of their entrance for a match against [[The League of Nations (professional wrestling)|The League of Nations]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Koch |first=Cameron |title=There Was 'Dragon Ball Z' Cosplay On Display At 'WrestleMania 32' |url=https://www.techtimes.com/articles/147087/20160404/there-was-dragonball-z-cosplay-on-display-at-wrestlemania-32.htm |work=Tech Times |date=April 4, 2016}}</ref> Argentine professional footballer [[Eduardo Salvio]] often celebrates his goals with gestures and signals referencing the signature attacks of various ''Dragon Ball'' characters.<ref>{{cite web |language=es|title=Eduardo Salvio y sus festejos al estilo de Dragon Ball |url=https://www.mediotiempo.com/futbol/eduardo-salvio-festejos-estilo-dragon-ball |work=Mediotiempo |date=September 18, 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |language=es|title=Los festejos de Eduardo Salvio en Boca, inspirados en Dragon Ball |url=https://www.clarin.com/deportes/boca-salvio-buffarini-festejo-dragonball_0_xmkUpvmF.html |work=Clarin |date=March 11, 2020}}</ref>

===Critical reception===
Carl Kimlinger of [[Anime News Network]] (ANN) stated, "Few anime series have mainstreamed it the way ''Dragon Ball Z'' has. To a certain generation of television consumers its characters are as well known as any in the animated realm, and for many it was the first step into the wilderness of anime fandom."<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/review/dragon-ball-z/dvd-dragon-box-z-set-2|title= Dragon Box Z Set 2|publisher=[[Anime News Network]]|date=2010-03-08|author= Kimlinger, Carl|access-date=2013-07-11}}</ref> His colleague Allen Divers praised the story and humor of the manga for being very good at conveying all of the characters' personalities.<ref>{{cite web|url= http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/review/dragon-ball-gn-5|title= Dragon Ball GN 5|publisher= [[Anime News Network]] |date= 2001-11-18 |author= Divers, Allen|access-date= 2008-09-27}}</ref> Carlo Santos, also from ANN, commented that the ''Dragon Ball'' cast "may not be as stylish-looking as today's [[Shōnen manga|shonen]] adventure protagonists, but every character has a distinctive set of physical features, making them identifiable at any moment".<ref name="ANNDBZGN12013">{{cite web|url= http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/review/dragon-ball-3-in-1-edition/gn-1|title= Dragon Ball [3-in-1 Edition] GN 1 – Review |publisher= [[Anime News Network]] |date= 2013-08-11 |author= Theron, Martin|access-date= 2015-03-12}}</ref> [[DVD Talk]]'s Todd Douglass praised the "deep, insightful, and well-developed" characters, writing "[f]ew shows can claim to have a cast quite like Dragon Ball's, and that's a testament to the creative genius of Toriyama."<ref>{{cite web|url= http://www.dvdtalk.com/reviews/38538/dragon-ball-season-one/|title= Dragon Ball: Season One|publisher=[[DVD Talk]] |author= Douglass Jr., Todd |date= 2009-09-15|access-date= 2015-03-10}}</ref> Tim Jones of T.H.E.M. Anime Reviews commended the series for having good characterization, saying: "You do care about them, and want to get to know more about them."<ref>{{cite web|url= http://www.themanime.org/viewreview.php?id=245|title= Dragon Ball Z anime review|publisher=themanime.org |author= Jones, Tim|access-date= 2013-07-11}}</ref> He considered them to be different from stereotypical stock characters, but noted that they have much more development early on than when compared to later in the series.<ref>{{cite web|url= http://www.themanime.org/viewreview.php?id=565|title= Dragon Ball anime review|publisher=themanime.org |author= Jones, Tim|access-date= 2008-10-03}}</ref>

Theron Martin, also from ANN, wrote that while the characters are not complicated, they are "easy to love, hate, and respect", and are a major reason for the series popularity. For example, he described the "immense pride of Vegeta", and how that can be a fatal flaw, especially shines through, as do the freewheeling spirits of Goten and Trunks, the naiveté of Buu and Mr. Satan's attention-loving, glory-hound nature, while Number 18 shows a cunning side.<ref>{{cite web |first= Theron|last= Martin|title=Dragon Ball – Season 8 Uncut (uncut)|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/review/dragon-ball-z/dvd-season-8|publisher=[[Anime News Network]]|date=4 March 2009|access-date= February 7, 2019}}</ref> He also praised the themes from the warriors, saying they speak to "basic yet powerful themes like faith, confidence, heroism, sacrifice, love, and understanding what is truly worth fighting for", and the ways they react while fighting, although the fights can sometimes become very long with little plot development.<ref name="ANNDBZS62008">{{cite web|url= http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/review/dragon-ball-z/dvd-season-6|title= Dragon Ball Z DVD Season 6 – Review|publisher= [[Anime News Network]] |date= 2008-11-25 |author= Theron, Martin|access-date= 2008-12-27}}</ref> On the other hand, the handling of the series' major female characters, such as Chi-Chi, Bulma and Videl, have been subject to some criticism.<ref name="HobbyConsolas">{{cite web |last1=Sánchez-Migallón|first1=Antonio|title=¿Dragon Ball es machista? El rol de la mujer en la serie|url=https://www.hobbyconsolas.com/opinion/dragon-ball-es-machista-rol-mujer-serie-98378|website=[[HobbyConsolas]]|language=Spanish |accessdate=April 9, 2021 |date=May 12, 2017}}</ref><ref name=Season8>{{cite web |first= Theron|last= Martin|title=Dragon Ball Z DVD – Season 8 Uncut |url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/review/dragon-ball-z/dvd-season-8|publisher=[[Anime News Network]]|date=25 November 2008|access-date= February 7, 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.fandompost.com/2014/03/13/dragon-ball-z-season-1-blu-ray-anime-review/|date=13 March 2014|title=Dragon Ball Z: Season 1 Blu-ray Anime Review|first=John|last=Begley}}</ref> Martin felt that the series overused the plot device of having characters "grow seemingly untouchably powerful, only to be put out when eventually upstaged".<ref name="ANNDBZS62008"/>

