===Other members===
;Genya Shinazugawa
:{{Voiced by|[[Nobuhiko Okamoto]]<ref name="staff2"/>|[[Zeno Robinson]]<ref>{{cite web|title=Genya Shinazugawa|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Genya-Shinazugawa/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=September 16, 2021|archive-date=September 16, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210916154226/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Genya-Shinazugawa/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:{{Nihongo|Genya Shinazugawa|不死川 玄弥|Shinazugawa Gen'ya}} is a Demon Slayer who cannot use breathing techniques. Instead, he possesses a unique ability to temporarily gain a demon's powers by consuming its flesh. He wields a shotgun that fires Nichirin steel pellets and a Nichirin wakizashi. He is the younger brother of the Wind Hashira, Sanemi Shinazugawa, and was in the same Final Selection as Tanjiro. Genya is mortally wounded during the battle against the Upper Rank Kokushibo, reconciling with his brother before his death.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Murata}}|村田|}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Kōki Miyata]]|[[Khoi Dao]]<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Dao, Khoi|number=1226384622851739648|user=khoidaooo|title=Hey #Toonami faithfuls. I have been waiting so long to tell you. I voice the goodest lad/secret protag/tiktok eboy MURATA in #DemonSlayer Murata stans of the world, our time has come. (thank you @BrianTAnderson for making this graphic i don't know why corporate rejected it)|date=February 8, 2020|access-date=February 17, 2022}}</ref>}}
:A member of the Demon Slayer Corps who is sent to Natagumo Mountain. He is one of the survivors of the operation to slay the Spider Family and befriends Tanjiro. Despite participating in the same Final Selection as Giyu, he lacks proven talent due to Sabito killing almost all of the demons, as well as the skill to become a Hashira like Giyu, but his determination motivates him to improve in Hashira Training, to the point he is able to defeat demons as powerful as the former Lower Ranks in the Infinity Castle. He survives the battle against Muzan and has a descendant who is a school principal.

==Demons==
{{Nihongo|Demons|鬼|[[Oni]]}} are a race of immortal creatures that feeds on blood to survive and become stronger with each human they devour. All demons were formerly humans who lost most of their memories and traces of humanity after drinking or being injected with Muzan's blood, becoming his servants and sharing their vision and thoughts with him. Demons possess enhanced senses, regeneration, and physical abilities. Higher demons are also capable of casting powerful spells called {{Nihongo|Blood Demon Arts|血鬼術|Kekkijutsu}}, which are unique to each demon.

Demons are weak to sunlight, which fatally turns them into ashes upon being exposed to it. They can also be killed by decapitation with special swords used by the Demon Slayers called {{Nihongo|Nichirin Swords|日輪刀|Nichirin Tō}}. Demons are also vulnerable to [[wisteria]] flowers, avoiding places where they are abundant and wisteria extract being poisonous to them in sufficient doses.

===Muzan Kibutsuji===
{{Main|Muzan Kibutsuji}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Toshihiko Seki]]<ref name="more-cast">{{cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Anime Reveals 4 More Cast Members in Video|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2019-05-05/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-reveals-4-more-cast-members-in-video/.146423|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=May 5, 2019|date=May 5, 2019|archive-date=May 9, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190509165800/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2019-05-05/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-reveals-4-more-cast-members-in-video/.146423|url-status=live}}</ref>|[[Greg Chun]]<ref name="English5" />}}

{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Muzan Kibutsuji}}|鬼舞辻 無惨|Kibutsuji Muzan}} is the first demon, originating from a failed experimental treatment during the Heian Period. He seeks to create a demon immune to sunlight to overcome his own weakness. This goal drives him to attack the Kamado family, resulting in Nezuko's transformation. When she later develops an immunity to sunlight, he becomes obsessed with consuming her to acquire it. During the final battle, he is weakened by a composite drug that suppresses his abilities and is ultimately destroyed by sunlight. In a final act of defiance, he transforms Tanjiro into a demon to be his successor, but he is thwarted when his friends successfully help turn him back to a human.

===Twelve Kizuki===
The {{Nihongo|Twelve Kizuki|十二鬼月|Jūnikizuki}} is a special group of demons who serve Muzan and have a special mark of their servitude engraved on their eyes. Second only to Muzan, they are the most powerful demons to have lived. The six weakest are known as the Lower Ranks and have a single eye engraved, while the six strongest are called the Upper Ranks and have both eyes engraved. After Rui's death, Muzan decides to eliminate the Lower Ranks and have only the Upper Ranks under his command.

====Upper Ranks====
The {{Nihongo|Upper Ranks|上弦|Jōgen}} are the high-ranking members of the Twelve Kizuki, with some having mutated their bodies to the point that, unlike other demons, they cannot be killed via decapitation. Their ranks were unaltered for over a century and no Demon Slayer had managed to kill any of them prior to Tanjiro and his friends joining the organization.

;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Kokushibo}}|黒死牟|Kokushibō}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Ryōtarō Okiayu]]<ref name="ANN-2023-02-03">{{cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|title=Man With a Mission, milet Perform Opening Theme for Demon Slayer Swordsmith Village Arc Anime|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-02-03/man-with-a-mission-milet-perform-opening-theme-for-demon-slayer-swordsmith-village-arc-anime/.194504|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=February 4, 2023|date=February 3, 2023|archive-date=February 3, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230203153629/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-02-03/man-with-a-mission-milet-perform-opening-theme-for-demon-slayer-swordsmith-village-arc-anime/.194504|url-status=live}}</ref>|[[Jonah Scott]]<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Scott, Jonah|number=1631809335855554562|user=ImMrTransistor|title=👁YO!!👁BIG NEWS!I CAN *FINALLY* SAY THAT I VOICE KOKUSHIBO IN DEMON SLAYER!!Thank you so much to the fans,@aniplexUSAand@mummynyanfor trusting me with such and important (and my favorite) character.I AM SO EXCITED TO JOIN THIS STELLAR CAST! IMMA MAKE YALL PROUD!|date=March 3, 2023|access-date=March 4, 2023}}</ref>}}
:Muzan's most powerful subordinate, who holds the title of Upper Rank One. As a human, he was a Demon Slayer named {{Nihongo|Michikatsu Tsugikuni|継国 巌勝|Tsugikuni Michikatsu}} and the older twin brother of Yoriichi. Envious of his brother's talent, he became a demon to perfect himself as a swordsman without the fear of death. As a transformed Demon Slayer, Kokushibo uses a breathing style known as {{Nihongo|"Moon Breathing"|月の呼吸|Tsuki no kokyū}}, which is derived from Yoriichi's Sun Breathing. He dies while fighting Muichiro, Genya, Sanemi, and Gyomei, with Muichiro and Genya dying from their wounds soon after.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Doma}}|童磨|Dōma}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Mamoru Miyano]]<ref>{{cite web|last=Pineda|first=Rafael|title=Demon Slayer: Entertainment District Arc Anime Finale Reveals Mamoru Miyano as Dōma|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2022-02-13/demon-slayer-entertainment-district-arc-anime-finale-reveals-mamoru-miyano-as-doma/.182590|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=February 14, 2022|date=February 13, 2022|archive-date=February 14, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220214020237/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2022-02-13/demon-slayer-entertainment-district-arc-anime-finale-reveals-mamoru-miyano-as-doma/.182590|url-status=live}}</ref>|Stephen Fu<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Stephen Fu|number=1520878656121278464|user=That_Fu|title=A mysterious Upper Six Demon has appeared! I'm SO excited to join #DemonSlayer! I'm also honored to be the english counterpart to the extremely talented Mamoru Miyano. Thanks so much for having me|date=May 1, 2022|access-date=May 1, 2022}}</ref>}}
:A nihilistic demon who holds the position of Upper Rank Two. As a human, Doma was born with rainbow-colored eyes and pale-blonde hair, which caused his parents to see him as perfect and blessed, and start a religious cult centered around him. After they died, he assumed control of the cult, and, after Muzan transformed him into a demon, began eating his followers under the belief that they would live forever inside him. One member of his cult was Inosuke's mother Kotoha, whom he devoured when she attempted to flee upon learning of his true nature. He was also responsible for killing Shinobu's older sister Kanae. In a desperate measure to defeat him, Shinobu administers a massive dose of wisteria-based poison in her body and allows herself to be consumed, weakening him and allowing Kanao and Inosuke to kill him.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Akaza}}|猗窩座}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Akira Ishida]]<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:『劇場版「鬼滅の刃」無限列車編』上弦の参の鬼・猗窩座役の石田彰さんら出演声優情報&コメント到着！ 煉?獄と猗窩座の戦いが描かれた新ビジュアル、新PV公開！|url=https://www.animatetimes.com/news/details.php?id=1603632279|website=[[Animate Times]]|access-date=August 3, 2021|date=October 25, 2020|language=ja|archive-date=October 24, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211024084254/https://www.animatetimes.com/news/details.php?id=1603632279|url-status=live}}</ref>|[[Lucien Dodge]]}}
:A contentious demon who holds the position of Upper Rank Three. He despises those he considers weak and offers those he considers strong enough to earn his respect the opportunity to become demons. As a human, he was a teenager named {{Nihongo|Hakuji|狛治}} who, as a child, stole to care for his ailing father before he committed suicide to free him from the burden of caring for him. Hakuji was adopted by a martial artist, Keizo, and trained under him while falling in love with his daughter Koyuki. Hakuji's adoptive family was killed when a rival dojo poisoned them, leading him to slaughter them single-handedly, after which Muzan turned him into a demon. Akaza battles and kills Kyojuro, and later battles Tanjiro and Giyu in the Infinity Castle, during which he regains his human memories and commits suicide by destroying his body and ceasing his regeneration, dying of his wounds.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Hantengu}}|半天狗}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Toshio Furukawa]] (original)<ref name="ANN-2023-02-03"/> [[Yūichirō Umehara]] (Sekido),<ref name="ANN-HantenguClones">{{cite web|last=Pineda|first=Rafael|title=Demon Slayer: Swordsmith Village Arc Anime Reveals Cast for Hantengu's Clones|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-04-23/demon-slayer-swordsmith-village-arc-anime-reveals-cast-for-hantengu-clones/.197404|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=April 24, 2023|date=April 23, 2023|archive-date=April 24, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230424012331/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-04-23/demon-slayer-swordsmith-village-arc-anime-reveals-cast-for-hantengu-clones/.197404|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Kaito Ishikawa]] (Karaku),<ref name="ANN-HantenguClones"/> [[Shunsuke Takeuchi]] (Urogi),<ref name="ANN-HantenguClones"/> [[Soma Saito]] (Aizetsu),<ref name="ANN-HantenguClones"/> [[Koichi Yamadera]] (Zohakuten)<ref>{{cite web|last=Pineda|first=Rafael|title=Demon Slayer: Swordsmith Village Arc Anime Casts Kōichi Yamadera as Zohakuten|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-05-21/demon-slayer-swordsmith-village-arc-anime-casts-koichi-yamadera-as-zohakuten/.198294|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=May 22, 2023|date=May 21, 2023|archive-date=May 22, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230522010511/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-05-21/demon-slayer-swordsmith-village-arc-anime-casts-koichi-yamadera-as-zohakuten/.198294|url-status=live}}</ref>|[[Christopher Corey Smith]] (original)<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (English)|number=1631806756757069824|user=DemonSlayerUSA|title=Presenting the English dub cast of the upper rank demons. 😨 Be the first to see them on the big screen in Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba -To the Swordsmith Village- now playing only in theaters! 🎟️ Get your tickets now: https://bit.ly/3HM3L7f|date=March 3, 2023|access-date=March 4, 2023}}</ref> Yong Yea (Sekido), Caleb Yen (Karaku), Chris Hackney (Urogi), Brian Timothy Anderson (Aizetsu), Ben Balmaceda (Zohakuten)}}
:A cowardly demon who holds the position of Upper Rank Four. Hantengu shows his true strength upon dividing himself into multiple clones which denote different emotions, each one possessing a unique appearance, personality, and ability: Sekido (anger), Karaku (pleasure), Aizetsu (sadness), Urogi (joy), Zohakuten (hatred), and Urami (resentment). As a human, he was a prolific criminal who boasted of his innocence despite his conviction before Muzan turned him into a demon. He attacks the Swordsmith Village with Gyokko, where Tanjiro, Nezuko, Genya, and Mitsuri confront him. Tanjiro kills him, but he lives long enough to inform Muzan of Nezuko's newfound immunity to sunlight.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Nakime}}|鳴女}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Marina Inoue]]<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:アニメ「鬼滅の刃」声優一覧 TVアニメ&劇場版出演の全キャスト170人を網羅|url=https://times.abema.tv/articles/-/8656684|website=[[Abema|Abema Times]]|access-date=March 4, 2023|language=ja|date=March 1, 2023|archive-date=March 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230304232913/https://times.abema.tv/articles/-/8656684|url-status=live}}</ref>|[[Amber Lee Connors]]}}
:A [[biwa]]-playing demon who owns the {{Nihongo|Infinity Castle|異空間無限城|Ikūkan Mugen-jō}}, an alternate dimensional space that Muzan made his base of operations. As a human, she was a struggling musician who developed a habit of murdering prior to her performances, as she associated killing with applause. She ended up meeting Muzan when she tried to kill him, only to earn his respect for tracking him and granting her new life as a demon. Nakime becomes Upper Rank Four after Hantengu's death and later confronts Mitsuri and Obanai until Yushiro restrains her, prompting Muzan to kill her to stop him from controlling the castle.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Gyokko}}|玉壼}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Kohsuke Toriumi]]<ref name="ANN-2023-02-03"/>|Brent Mukai<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Bukai, Brent|number=1632127931647655936|user=brentmukai|title=The news is out! I play Gyokko in the Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba – To the Swordsmith Village Movie! Now out in theaters! I'm going to see it today, so excited!!!|date=March 4, 2023|access-date=March 4, 2023}}</ref>}}
:An arrogant demon holds the position of Upper Rank Five. Unlike the others, Gyokko has a highly distorted djinn-like anatomy with his eyes being on his forehead and mouth along with two mouths being where his eyes would be. As a human, he was an ostracized villager who developed an obsession with corpses after his parents drowned at sea and their bodies washed up on shore. He kidnapped and killed a child before being stabbed and left for dead, after which Muzan transformed him into a demon. He claims himself to be an artist and takes pride in his creations, including twisting his victims' bodies into grotesque, living sculptures. He attacks the Swordsmith Village alongside Hantengu but is killed by Muichiro.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Daki}}|堕姫}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Miyuki Sawashiro]]<ref>{{cite web|last=Loo|first=Egan|title=Demon Slayer Anime Unveils New Cast, Songs by LiSA & Aimer, Entertainment District Arc's December 5 Debut, 7-Episode Mugen Train TV Version|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2021-09-25/demon-slayer-anime-unveils-new-cast-songs-by-lisa-and-aimer-entertainment-district-arc-december-5-/.177823|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=January 17, 2022|date=September 25, 2021|archive-date=December 1, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211201075341/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2021-09-25/demon-slayer-anime-unveils-new-cast-songs-by-lisa-and-aimer-entertainment-district-arc-december-5-/.177823|url-status=live}}</ref>|[[Erica Lindbeck]]<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (English)|number=1499776906857701377|user=DemonSlayerUSA|title=#NEWS Introducing the English voice of Daki (Upper Six) in Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Entertainment District Arc – Erica Lindbeck (@ericalindbeck)! ✨|date=March 4, 2022|access-date=March 4, 2022}}</ref>}}
:A petulant demon who shares the position of Upper Rank Six with her older brother Gyutaro. Daki takes advantage of her work as an [[oiran]] in the red-light district to attract victims. As a human, she was named {{Nihongo|Ume|梅||lit. [[syphilis]]}}, after the disease that killed her mother, and was raised by Gyutaro in the district slums they were born in. Her beauty led to success in the district at a young age, until she was burned alive at the age of thirteen by a customer she attacked. She was on the verge of dying alongside Gyutaro when Doma – who was Upper Rank Six then – transformed and introduced them to the Twelve Kizuki. She wields an obi belt made of her flesh, which she also uses to absorb her victims and place them in a hidden cave before devouring them. After Zenitsu and Inosuke kill her, she returns to her former human appearance and meets Gyutaro in the afterlife, refusing to leave his side despite him trying to push her away so she would not have to go to Hell, reminding him of their promise to survive anything together.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Gyutaro}}|妓夫太郎|Gyūtarō}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Ryōta Ōsaka]]<ref>{{cite web|last=Mateo|first=Alex|title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Entertainment District Arc Anime Casts Ryota Ohsaka|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2022-01-17/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-entertainment-district-arc-anime-casts-ryota-ohsaka/.181607|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=January 17, 2022|date=January 17, 2022|archive-date=January 17, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220117183914/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2022-01-17/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-entertainment-district-arc-anime-casts-ryota-ohsaka/.181607|url-status=live}}</ref>|[[Brandon McInnis]]<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (English)|number=1508791388426625032|user=DemonSlayerUSA|title=#NEWS Introducing the English voice of Gyutaro (Upper Six) in Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Entertainment District Arc – Brandon McInnis (@BranMci)! ✨|date=March 29, 2022|access-date=March 29, 2022}}</ref>}}
:A misanthropic demon who shares the position of Upper Rank Six with his younger sister Daki. As a human, he was born in the red-light district slums alongside Daki and was ostracized for his unsightly appearance. Ume gave him joy and allowed him to embrace his vile disposition while making a living as a debt collector, only to be mortally wounded after killing the customer who burned her alive; Doma later turned him into a demon. He usually hides within Daki's body and emerges whenever her life is threatened. He fights using his poisonous blood and two flesh sickles as his Blood Demon Art. As dual holders of Upper Rank Six, Gyutaro must be decapitated together with Daki to be truly killed. After Tengen and Tanjiro kill him, he expresses regret over being a negative influence to Ume when she was alive and decides to go to Hell alone to atone for their sins, but he relents after Ume refuses to leave his side.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Kaigaku}}|獪岳}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Yoshimasa Hosoya]]|[[Alejandro Saab]]<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Saab, Alejandro|number=1231458892170719233|user=kaggyfilms|title=Thank you guys for watching #DemonSlayer it truly is incredible getting to be a part of this, even if it is a small part (for now ) And as much as I tease him, @AleksLeVO absolutely KILLS IT as Zenitsu! Thank you again to @aniplexUSA @mummynyan and @BangZoom for having me!!|date=February 23, 2020|access-date=February 17, 2022}}</ref>}}
:A young demon who becomes the new Upper Rank Six following Daki and Gyutaro's deaths. As a human, he was one of the orphans under Gyomei's care; he was chased out by the other children for stealing the temple's money and encountered a demon, which he let into the temple in exchange for having his life spared, leading to their deaths and Gyomei's wrongful imprisonment. He then became a member of the Demon Slayer Corps, learning the Thunder Breathing style from Jigoro along with Zenitsu, before betraying them and allowing Kokushibo to transform him into a demon, leading Jigoro to commit seppuku in atonement. Unlike Zenitsu, who only mastered the first of the six forms of Thunder Breathing, Kaigaku only mastered the other five. He battles Zenitsu but is killed when Zenitsu strikes him with a self-taught, seventh form.

====Lower Ranks====
The {{Nihongo|Lower Ranks|下弦|Kagen}} of the Twelve Kizuki, whose membership is constantly shifting compared to the Upper Ranks. Following Rui's death, Muzan kills all of them except for Emmu for being worthless to his plans.

;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Enmu}}|魘夢}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Daisuke Hirakawa]]<ref name="Enmu"/>|Landon McDonald<ref name="Enmu">{{cite web|title=Enmu (Lower One) Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Enmu-Lower-One|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003208/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Enmu-Lower-One/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A sadistic demon who holds the position of Lower Rank One and is the main antagonist of the ''Mugen Train'' arc. He is intensely devoted to Muzan, having rose up to his current status to be acknowledged by him. As a human, he was a delusional sociopath who pretended to be a healer to swindle people out of their money and was transformed into a demon by Muzan, who originally intended to eat him. His Blood Demon Art allows him to manipulate a person's dreams and nightmares. Being the only Lower Rank that Muzan spared after he slaughtered the others, Enmu is tasked with killing the Hashira and Tanjiro. He lays a trap for Tanjiro and his friends on the Mugen Train, that he later fuses himself to, but Tanjiro kills him.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Rui}}|累}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Kōki Uchiyama]]|[[Billy Kametz]]<ref name="English7">{{Cite web|last=Mateo|first=Alex|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2020-02-05/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-reveals-more-english-dub-cast-english-trailer/.156151|title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Anime Reveals More English Dub Cast, English Trailer|website=[[Anime News Network]]|date=February 5, 2020|access-date=February 5, 2020|archive-date=February 6, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200206065137/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2020-02-05/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-reveals-more-english-dub-cast-english-trailer/.156151|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A child-like demon who holds the position of Lower Rank Five. As a human, he was a sickly boy who was transformed by Muzan. He killed his parents in self-defense when they attempted to kill him out of atonement; the ordeal caused Rui to forget his human memories. Being a favoured member of the Twelve Kizuki, he gains Muzan's permission to transform other humans and demons with his blood into a replacement family, who he abuses due to his warped view of familial bonds. This causes him to be envious of the Kamado siblings' bond, as he loses his calm demeanor and attacks erratically until Giyu kills him. In his final moments, he remembers his parents and reunites with them in Hell.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Kyogai}}|響凱|Kyōgai}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Junichi Suwabe]]<ref>{{cite web|last=Pineda|first=Rafael Antonio|title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Anime Casts Junichi Suwabe|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2019-06-09/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-casts-junichi-suwabe/.147668|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=June 9, 2019|date=June 9, 2019|archive-date=June 10, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190610081728/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2019-06-09/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-casts-junichi-suwabe/.147668|url-status=live}}</ref>|[[Steve Blum]]<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (English)|number=1215000672476782594|user=DemonSlayerUSA|title=ENGLISH CAST ANNOUNCEMENT! The legendary @blumspew joins the English dub cast as the Tsuzumi Demon, Kyogai! Tune in for Episode 11 of Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba this Saturday on Cartoon Network's Toonami!|date=January 8, 2020|access-date=February 17, 2022}}</ref>}}
:A demon and former Lower Rank Six of the Twelve Kizuki. He is known as the {{Nihongo|"Drum Demon"|鼓鬼|[[Tsuzumi]] Oni}}. After Muzan strips him of his rank due to slowly losing the ability to eat humans and reaching his limit, he obsessively tries to earn his spot back in the Twelve Kizuki, attacking and eating humans who pass by the Tsuzumi Mansion. He fights using the tsuzumi drums embedded into his body; striking them can change the house's rooms around as well as his position in it, and also allows him to unleash powerful air slashes. Following an arduous battle, Tanjiro kills him.
;{{Nihongo|Kamanue|釜鵺}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Kenn (actor)|KENN]]|Alan Lee<ref>{{cite web|title=Kamanue (Lower Six) Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Kanamori/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 5, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003221/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Kanamori/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A demon who holds the position of Lower Rank Six. He is the first member of the Lower Ranks that Muzan kills when he decides to purge the Lower Ranks after he questions his expectations, which Muzan sees as defiance.
;{{Nihongo|Mukago|零余子}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Kana Ueda]]<ref name="Mukago"/>|[[Kira Buckland]]<ref name="Mukago">{{cite web|title=Mukago (Lower Four) Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Mukago-Lower-Four|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003309/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Mukago-Lower-Four/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A demon who holds the position of Lower Rank Four. Muzan kills her after deducing that she was more afraid of the Demon Slayers than him and interpreted her attempt at saving face as contradicting him.
;{{Nihongo|Wakuraba|病葉}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Sōichirō Hoshi]]<ref name="Wakuraba"/>|Emma Martello<ref name="Wakuraba">{{cite web|title=Wakuraba (Lower Three) Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Wakuraba-Lower-Three|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003234/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Wakuraba-Lower-Three/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A demon who holds the position of Lower Rank Three. Muzan kills him when he tries to escape the Infinity Castle.
;{{Nihongo|Rokuro|轆轤}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Taiten Kusunoki]]<ref name="Rokuro"/>|[[Ray Chase (voice actor)|Ray Chase]]<ref name="Rokuro">{{cite web|title=Rokuro (Lower Two) Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Rokuro-Lower-Two|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003301/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Rokuro-Lower-Two/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A demon who holds the position of Lower Rank Two. He is killed when he asks Muzan for his blood to gain strength and fight for him, which Muzan saw as undermining his authority.

===Spider Family===
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Spider Demon (Mother)}}|蜘蛛鬼「母」|Kumo Oni: Haha}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Ami Koshimizu]]|[[Allegra Clark]]}}<ref name="English7" />
:A member of the Spider Family. As a human, she was a young girl who was turned into a demon, with Rui later forcing her to assume the role of "Mother" and have her appearance altered. She can control her victims like puppets using her silk threads, which are attached to them by small white spiders; her strongest weapon is a headless demon corpse with scythe-like arms. She lives in great fear of Rui, and ultimately allows Tanjiro to slay her when they fight, allowing her to be free.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Spider Demon (Father)}}|蜘蛛鬼「父」|Kumo Oni: Chichi}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Tetsu Inada]]|[[Kellen Goff]]}}<ref name="English7" />
:A member of the Spider Family, who assumes the role of "Father". Unlike the rest of his family, his appearance is less human, possessing a spider's head atop a giant humanoid body. He attacks Tanjiro and Inosuke, until he is killed when Giyu intervenes.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Spider Demon (Brother)}}|蜘蛛鬼「兄」|Kumo Oni: Ani}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Showtaro Morikubo]]|[[Derek Stephen Prince]]}}<ref name="English7" />
:A member of the Spider Family, who assumes the role of "Elder Brother" and is one of the two in the family that does not look human, possessing a human head and a spider's body. He has the ability to turn humans into monstrous semi-spiders when his minions bite them. He is ultimately killed by Zenitsu.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Spider Demon (Sister)}}|蜘蛛鬼「姉」|Kumo Oni: Ane}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Ryōko Shiraishi]]|[[Erica Lindbeck]]}}<ref name="English7" />
:A member of the Spider Family, who assumed the role of "Elder Sister" after begging Rui for safety from the Demon Slayers. She has the ability to create acidic cocoons of thread that dissolve her victims and convert them into food. She nearly kills Murata, but Shinobu subdues and kills her.

===Other Demons===
;{{Nihongo|Temple Demon|お堂の鬼|Odō no Oni}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Hikaru Midorikawa]]<ref name="staff2"/>|[[Benjamin Diskin|Ben Diskin]]<ref>{{cite web|title=Demon in the Temple – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Demon-in-the-Temple|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003304/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Demon-in-the-Temple/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A demon who Tanjiro and Nezuko briefly encounter and defeat together.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Hand Demon}}|手鬼|Te Oni}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Takehito Koyasu]], [[Aki Toyosaki]]<ref>{{cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Anime Casts Takehito Koyasu, Aki Toyosaki as Hand Demon|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2019-04-27/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-casts-takehito-koyasu-aki-toyosaki-as-hand-demon/.146207|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=April 27, 2019|date=April 27, 2019|archive-date=April 27, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190427054300/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2019-04-27/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-casts-takehito-koyasu-aki-toyosaki-as-hand-demon/.146207|url-status=live}}</ref> (child)|[[Kirk Thornton]],<ref>{{cite web|title=Hand Demon Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Hand-Demon|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230304232943/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Hand-Demon/|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Jessica DiCicco]]<ref>{{cite web|title=Hand Demon (Boy) Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Hand-Demon-Boy|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003208/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Hand-Demon-Boy/|url-status=live}}</ref> (child)}}
:A vengeful demon who Sakonji captured and trapped on a mountain and was used for testing applicants for the Demon Slayer Corps. Unable to escape the mountain, he made it his goal to target and eat Sakonji's disciples as revenge, until he was eventually killed by Tanjiro.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Swamp Demon}}|沼鬼|Numa Oni}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Ryōhei Kimura]]<ref name="more-cast"/>|[[Sean Chiplock]]<ref name="English5">{{cite tweet|author=[[Aniplex of America]]|number=1195069199070236672|user=aniplexUSA|title=Meet the Demons of "Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba" and Tanjiro's greatest foe, Muzan Kibutsuji! Don't forget! A new episode of the English dub of "Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba" airs every Saturday night at 1:30 am only on Cartoon Network's Toonami!|date=November 14, 2019|access-date=February 17, 2022}}</ref>}}
:A demon responsible for the disappearance of several girls, who he prefers to be under the age of 16 or else they would "become rotten". He is the target of Tanjiro's first assignment as a Demon Slayer, and is killed by him.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Yahaba}}|矢琶羽}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Jun Fukuyama]]<ref name="more-cast"/>|[[Xander Mobus]]<ref name="English5" />}}
:A demon who serves Muzan and falsely believes that he is one of the Twelve Kizuki. He has the ability to manipulate the movement and direction of midair objects using the eyeballs on his palms to control telekinetic arrows. He is killed by Tanjiro.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Susamaru}}|朱紗丸}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Mikako Komatsu]]<ref name="more-cast"/>|[[Sarah Anne Williams|Sarah Ann Williams]]<ref name="English5" />}}
:A demon who serves Muzan and falsely believes that she is one of the Twelve Kizuki. She has the ability to sprout multiple arms and create special [[Temari (toy)|Temari]], using them as projectile weapons in conjunction with Yahaba's ability. She is defeated when Tamayo uses her hypnosis to trick her into triggering Muzan's curse, causing her body to destroy itself.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Tongue Demon}}|舌鬼|Shita Oni}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Tarusuke Shingaki]]<ref name="more-cast"/>|}}
:A demon that lived in the Tsuzumi Mansion. He has four eyes and a long prehensile tongue that functions as a bladed weapon. He argued with Kyogai and the Horned Demon over the right to kill a boy Kyogai caught. He was killed by Zenitsu.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Horned Demon}}|角状鬼|Tsunojō Oni}}
:{{Voiced by|Yoshihisa Kawahara}}
:A demon that lived in the Tsuzumi Mansion. He was obese and slow for a demon. He argued with the Tongue Demon and Kyogai over the right to kill a boy Kyogai caught, ultimately ripping off one of his tsuzumi drums. He was killed by Inosuke.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Slasher}}|切きり裂さき|Kirisaki}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Kentarō Itō]]}}
:The nickname given to a sadistic and cruel demon that appeared during the investigation of the Mugen Train and was responsible for attacking humans until Kyojuro killed him. He is exclusive to the anime, only appearing in Episode 27.

==Kamado family==
The Kamado family is a line of charcoal makers and the descendants of Sumiyoshi, a close friend of Yoriichi Tsugikuni and the progenitor of the Hinokami Kagura, which was made as a promise to preserve his Sun Breathing through his descendants. After Muzan murdered them in an attempt to sire a sunlight-immune demon, its sole survivors are Tanjiro and Nezuko.

;{{Nihongo|Tanjuro Kamado|竈門 炭十郎|Kamado Tanjūrō}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Shinichiro Miki]]<ref name="Tanjuro"/>|[[Kirk Thornton]]<ref name="Tanjuro">{{cite web|title=Hand Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Tanjuro-Kamado/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003246/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Tanjuro-Kamado/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:The husband of Kie and father of Tanjiro and Nezuko, who Tanjiro inherited his earrings and the Hinokami Kagura from. Despite his frail body and illness, Tanjuro was skilled at using the style, never tiring during his yearly night-long dance in frigid weather and being able to decapitate a large bear with ease.
;{{Nihongo|Kie Kamado|竈門 葵枝|Kamado Kie}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Houko Kuwashima]]<ref name="Kie"/>|[[Dorothy Elias-Fahn]]<ref name="Kie">{{cite web|title=Kie Kamado Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Kie-Kamado/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003318/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Kie-Kamado/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:Tanjuro's wife and mother of Tanjiro and Nezuko. After her husband's death, she was left to take care of them by herself, with Tanjiro helping her. She managed to support and keep her family happy until her death.
;{{Nihongo|Takeo Kamado|竈門 竹雄|Kamado Takeo}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Yō Taichi]]<ref name="Takeo"/>|[[Michelle Ruff]]<ref name="Takeo">{{cite web|title=Takeo Kamado Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Takeo-Kamado/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003250/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Takeo-Kamado/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:The third child of the Kamado family and Tanjiro's first younger brother. Unlike his family, he is more reserved and introverted.
;{{Nihongo|Hanako Kamado|竈門 花子|Kamado Hanako}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Konomi Kohara]]<ref name="Hanako"/>|Ryan Bartley<ref name="Hanako">{{cite web|title=Hanako Kamado Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Hanako-Kamado/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003206/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Hanako-Kamado/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:The fourth child of the Kamado family and Tanjiro's second younger sister. She adored him and wanted to follow him when he left to sell charcoal, but Kie forbid her from leaving. Tanjiro told her to wait for him until he returned, but was killed by the time he returned.
;{{Nihongo|Shigeru Kamado|竈門 茂|Kamado Shigeru}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Kaede Hondo]]<ref name="Shigeru"/>|[[Jessica DiCicco]]<ref name="Shigeru">{{cite web|title=Shigeru Kamado Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Shigeru-Kamado/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003321/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Shigeru-Kamado/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:The fifth child of the Kamado family. Like Hanako, he adored Tanjiro and wanted to follow him, but was killed by the time he returned.
;{{Nihongo|Rokuta Kamado|竈門 六太|Kamado Rokuta}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Aoi Koga]]<ref name="Rokuta"/>|[[Philece Sampler]]<ref name="Rokuta">{{cite web|title=Rokuta Kamado Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Rokuta-Kamado/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003311/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Rokuta-Kamado/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:The youngest child of the Kamado family, who was killed despite Nezuko trying to protect him. She is often reminded of him when she sees other humans.
;{{Nihongo|Sumiyoshi|炭吉}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Hirofumi Nojima]]|[[Howard Wang]]}}
:An ancestor of the Kamado family who was friends with Yoriichi Tsugikuni, the creator of Sun Breathing, and developed the Hinokami Kagura based on a demonstration Yoriichi made to him and his family. He also received from Yoriichi the Hanafuda earrings which Tanjiro wears.
;{{Nihongo|Sumihiko Kamado|竈門 炭彦|Kamado Sumihiko}}
:A 15-year-old boy who is Tanjiro and Kanao's descendant in modern times and resembles Tanjiro.
;{{Nihongo|Kanata Kamado|竈門 カナタ|Kamado Kanata}}
:A 16-year-old boy and one of Tanjiro and Kanao's descendants in modern times. He is Sumihiko's older brother and resembles Kanao.

==Rengoku family==
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Shinjuro Rengoku}}|煉獄 槇寿郎|Rengoku Shinjurō}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Rikiya Koyama]]|Imari Williams<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Williams, Imari|number=1385790385813803009|user=ImariSpeaks|title=So freaking PUMPED to announce this. I had the honor and privilege of lending my voice to #DemonSlayerMovie #MugenTrain! I play #ShinjuroRengoku and a couple of other characters. So thankful to @BangZoom for allowing me this opportunity. This one of my favorite franchises|date=April 23, 2021|access-date=February 17, 2022}}</ref>}}
:The former Flame Hashira and father of Kyojuro and Senjuro. After his wife's death, he spiraled into depression and rejected his duties as Flame Hashira, becoming resentful of the Demon Slayer Corps. Since then, he spends his days drinking at home until he receives Kyojuro's final message, asking him to take care of himself. During the final battle against Muzan, he protects the Ubuyashiki family alongside Tengen.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Ruka Rengoku}}|煉獄 瑠火|Rengoku Ruka}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Megumi Toyoguchi]]|[[Suzie Yeung]]<ref name="Yeung"/>}}
:Shinjuro's late wife and mother of Kyojuro and Senjuro, who instilled in Kyojuro his moral code to use his strength to protect the weak.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Senjuro Rengoku}}|煉獄 千寿郎|Rengoku Senjurō}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Junya Enoki]]|Cedric Williams<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Williams, Cedric|number=1385413271650324481|user=cedwilliamsjr|title=God is so good! The dub for #DemonSlayer #MugenTrain is finally in theaters everywhere & I'm proud to announce that I'm the English voice of Senjuro Rengoku. Super grateful to be a small part in this epic movie. Thank you @mummynyan & @aniplexUSA for the opportunity!|date=April 22, 2021|access-date=February 17, 2022}}</ref>}}
:Kyojuro's younger brother, who befriends Tanjiro and begins researching what documents remain from his estate about the Hinokami Kagura and its connection with Sun Breathing. He later sends a letter to Tanjiro describing a thirteenth, lost technique from the Hinokami Kagura, hoping it will help him in his battle against Muzan.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor| Tojuro Rengoku}}|煉獄 桃寿郎|Rengoku Tōjurō}}
:The modern descendant of the Rengoku family, who is similar to Kyojuro in appearance and personality and is a close friend of Sumihiko.

==Supporting characters==
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Sakonji Urokodaki}}|鱗滝 左近次|Urokodaki Sakonji}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Hōchū Ōtsuka]]<ref name="staff2">{{cite web|last=Loo|first=Egan|title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Anime Reveals More Cast, Theme Song Artist|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2019-03-19/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-reveals-more-cast-theme-song-artist/.144726|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=March 19, 2019|date=March 19, 2019|archive-date=June 7, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190607192533/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2019-03-19/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-reveals-more-cast-theme-song-artist/.144726|url-status=live}}</ref>|Brook Chalmers<ref>{{cite web|title=Sakonji Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Sakonji-Urokodaki/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003225/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Sakonji-Urokodaki/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A former Water Hashira. After his successor Giyu introduces him to Tanjiro and Nezuko, he is initially apprehensive due to Tanjiro's kind nature, but agrees to train him. Over the course of training, he grows closer to both Tanjiro and Nezuko, and is overjoyed when Tanjiro returns from Final Selection, as he is the first to do so after a long string of deaths. He gave his word to the Hashira that if Nezuko were to eat a human, then he, Giyu, and Tanjiro would kill her and themselves in atonement.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Sabito}}|錆兎}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Yūki Kaji]]<ref name="staff2"/>|[[Max Mittelman]]<ref name="English2">{{cite tweet|author=[[Aniplex of America]]|number=1187519263592144898|user=aniplexUSA|title=[ENGLISH DUB CAST ANNOUNCEMENT] @MaxMittelman and @RyanBartley join the English dub cast of Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba as Sabito and Makomo! Catch them in action on Episode 3 – "Sabito and Makomo" this Saturday night at 1:30 AM on @cartoonnetwork ! #DemonSlayer|date=October 24, 2019|access-date=February 17, 2022}}</ref>}}
:One of Sakonji's disciples, who was noted for his skill and strength. He befriended Giyu, teaching him to value his life as a gift from his older sister, who saved him from a demon. During Final Selection, while trying to save entrants who were not as strong as him, he was killed by the Hand Demon as revenge for Sakonji's capture of him. His spirit later advises Tanjiro during his training. 
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Makomo}}|真菰}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Ai Kakuma]]<ref name="staff2"/>|Ryan Bartley<ref name="English2" />}}
:One of Sakonji's disciples, who, like Sabito, was highly skilled, noted to have great speed and agility in battle. She was killed by the Hand Demon during Final Selection, and her spirit later advises Tanjiro during his training. 
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Kasugai Crows}}|鎹鴉|Kasugai Garasu}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Takumi Yamazaki]] (Tanjiro's),<ref name="staff2"/> [[Rie Kugimiya]] (Muichiro's)<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:『鬼滅の刃』無一郎の鎹鴉役は釘宮理恵|url=https://www.oricon.co.jp/news/2275674/full/|website=[[Oricon|Oricon News]]|access-date=May 10, 2023|language=ja|date=April 16, 2023|archive-date=April 24, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230424005954/https://www.oricon.co.jp/news/2275674/full/|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Show Hayami]] (Kagaya's)|[[Doug Erholtz]]<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Erholtz, Doug|number=1416084466867396608|user=dougerholtz|title=Kasugai Crow... the most charismatic of all birds, will be perched on youtube tomorrow for a free panel.Come check it out!Caw Caw!!!!|date=July 16, 2021|access-date=March 4, 2023}}</ref>}}
:Crows that can speak human language and accompany Demon Slayers, informing them of new missions.
;{{Nihongo|Ukogi|うこぎ}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Manaka Iwami]]|[[Abby Trott]]}}
:A sparrow who was the only one of his species to pass the exam to work as a Kasugai Crow. He was assigned to Zenitsu, who nicknames him {{Nihongo|Chuntaro|チュン太郎|Chuntarō}}, and usually reprimands him when he shows cowardice.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Tamayo}}|珠世}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Maaya Sakamoto]]<ref name="cast3">{{cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Anime Casts Maaya Sakamoto, Daiki Yamashita|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2019-05-19/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-casts-maaya-sakamoto-daiki-yamashita/.146885|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=May 19, 2019|date=May 19, 2019|archive-date=August 12, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200812214452/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2019-05-19/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-anime-casts-maaya-sakamoto-daiki-yamashita/.146885|url-status=live}}</ref>|[[Laura Post]]<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Post, Laura|number=1203061848427266048|user=laurapostvoice|title=Very excited to be joining the cast of Demon Slayer as Tamayo! If you're not watching, you should be! It's gorgeous!|date=December 6, 2019|access-date=March 4, 2023}}</ref>}}
:A demon who works as a doctor. Muzan transformed her into a demon, resulting in her killing and eating her family, and being under his control until he was almost killed by Yoriichi, who spared her. She altered herself to allow her to survive on small amounts of blood, not human flesh. She seeks to find a cure for demons, which requires the blood of higher demons for her to study on, and enlists Tanjiro to help her, who offers some of Nezuko's blood and attains blood samples from members of the Twelve Kizuki. She is the only demon besides Muzan who can create demons, but insists on only doing it for dying patients who have no other option and ensures they know the price of becoming a demon. After completing her research on a cure for Nezuko's transformation, Tamayo sacrifices herself to lay an ambush on Muzan with Kagaya's help, poisoning him and weakening him enough to be killed.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Yushiro}}|愈史郎|Yushirō}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Daiki Yamashita]]<ref name="cast3" />|[[Kyle McCarley]]<ref>{{cite tweet|author=McCarley, Kyle|number=1203432253201604608|user=KyleMcCarley|title=Catch me on #DemonSlayer on Toonami as one of the good guy demons: Yushiro!|date=December 7, 2019|access-date=March 4, 2023}}</ref>}}
:A demon created by Tamayo, who cares for and is deeply protective of her. Like Tamayo, he survives on small amounts of blood, even less than her. He is mentioned to have a "battle form" that he can transform into, and uses paper talismans to share his sight with others, conceal the presence of living things and objects, and reveal what is normally unseen. Following Tamayo's death, Yushiro assists the Demon Slayers in the final battle against Muzan by providing aid to the wounded, battling Nakime, and helping Tanjiro and his friends evade Muzan with his talismans. After Muzan's defeat, Yushiro continues living as a demon to modern times, where he becomes a world-renowned painter.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Jigoro Kuwajima}}|桑島 慈悟郎|Kuwajima Jigorō}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Shigeru Chiba]]<ref name="Jigoro"/>|[[John DeMita]]<ref name="Jigoro">{{cite web|title=Jigoro Kuwajima Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Jigoro-Kuwajima/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003207/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Jigoro-Kuwajima/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A former Thunder Hashira who served as the instructor for Zenitsu and Kaigaku. He committed seppuku in atonement for Kaigaku's betrayal, which becomes Zenitsu's motivation to find and kill him.
;{{Nihongo|Kotoha Hashibira|嘴平 琴葉|Hashibira Kotoha}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Mamiko Noto]]|[[Jennie Kwan]]<ref>{{cite episode|title=A Forged Bond|series=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba|date=February 29, 2020|number=18|time=Closing credits, English Language Cast|location=USA|series-link=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba|network=Adult Swim|season=1}}</ref>}}
:Inosuke's late mother, who was killed by Doma just before dropping Inosuke from a cliff to save his life.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Makio}}|まきを}}{{nobold|,}} {{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Suma}}|須磨}} {{nobold|and}} {{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Hinatsuru}}|雛鶴}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Shizuka Ishigami]] (Makio), [[Nao Tōyama]] (Suma), [[Atsumi Tanezaki]] (Hinatsuru)<ref>{{cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|title=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Entertainment District Arc Anime Reveals Cast for Tengen Uzui's Wives|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2021-12-06/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-entertainment-district-arc-anime-reveals-cast-for-tengen-uzui-wives/.180330|website=Anime News Network|access-date=December 6, 2021|date=December 6, 2021|archive-date=December 6, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211206111659/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2021-12-06/demon-slayer-kimetsu-no-yaiba-entertainment-district-arc-anime-reveals-cast-for-tengen-uzui-wives/.180330|url-status=live}}</ref>|[[Erica Mendez]] (Makio), [[Emi Lo]] (Suma), [[Anairis Quiñones]] (Hinatsuru)<ref>{{cite tweet|author=Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (English)|number=1498327136645496834|user=DemonSlayerUSA|title=Introducing the #EnglishDub cast of Tengen Uzui's flashy wives in Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Entertainment District Arc:✨ Makio: Erica Mendez (@tsunderica)✨ Suma: Emi Lo (@KitsuneSqueak)✨ Hinatsuru: Anairis Quiñones (@anairis_q)|date=February 28, 2022|access-date=February 28, 2022}}</ref>}}
:[[kunoichi|Kuoichi]]s and Tengen's wives, who assist him on his mission to Yoshiwara. When they go missing, Tengen enlists the help of Tanjiro and his friends to find them. Suma and Makio are freed by Inosuke, and Hinatsuru is found by Tengen after she tried to flee from Daki.
;{{Nihongo|Yoriichi Tsugikuni|継国 縁壱|Tsugikuni Yoriichi}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Kazuhiko Inoue]]|Mick Lauer}}
:Kokushibo's younger twin brother, who was born with a mark that gave him enhanced perception and physical abilities; he later became a Demon Slayer after a demon killed his pregnant wife. He is the creator of Sun Breathing, which branched into other styles. As a Demon Slayer, he cornered and nearly defeated Muzan, but failed to destroy him despite inflicting multiple wounds on him that never healed. He was banished from the Corps for his failure to kill Muzan and Michikatsu's betrayal. He later befriended Tanjiro's ancestors and taught them Sun Breathing, which they passed on to their lineage in the form of the Hinokami Kagura, along with the hanafuda earrings Tanjiro now wears. He died of old age during a fight with Kokushibo.

==Minor characters==
;{{Nihongo|Saburo|三郎|Saburō}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Masaki Terasoma]]<ref name="Saburo"/>|Jake Eberle<ref name="Saburo">{{cite web|title=Saburo Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Saburo/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003214/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Saburo/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A villager who offers Tanjiro to stay at his home the night his family is killed out of fear for his safety. He is afraid of demons because his family was killed by them.
;{{Nihongo|Toyo|豊}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Mitsuo Iwata]]<ref name="Toyo"/>|Frank Todaro<ref name="Toyo">{{cite web|title=Toyo Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Toyo/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003235/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Toyo/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:An udon street vendor from Asakusa who is passionate about udon and is angered when his customers discard their bowls without eating any. He becomes angry with Tanjiro when he flees to pursue Muzan, but is pleased after he returns and eats two bowls of udon to make up for it.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Teruko}}|照子}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Miho Okasaki]]<ref name="Teruko"/>|Grace Lu<ref name="Teruko">{{cite web|title=Teruko Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Teruko/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003204/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Teruko/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A young girl, who, along with her brother Shoichi, asks Tanjiro and Zenitsu to help save her missing brother Kiyoshi from the Tsuzumi Mansion. She enters the mansion in Tanjiro's company, where they find Kiyoshi and Kyogai, upon which, Tanjiro orders them to leave as he prepares to face the demon.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Shoichi}}|正一|Shōichi}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Mitsuhiro Ichiki]]<ref name="Shoichi"/>|[[Michael Johnston (actor)|Michael Johnston]]<ref name="Shoichi">{{cite web|title=Shoichi Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Shoichi/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003209/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Shoichi/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:A young boy, who, along with his sister Teruko, asks Tanjiro and Zenitsu to help save her brother Kiyoshi from the Tsuzumi Mansion. When he is separated from his siblings inside the mansion, he winds up in Zenitsu's company. When Zenitsu kills one of the demons pursuing them in his sleep, he believes Shoichi is the one who saved his life when they escape the mansion.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Kiyoshi}}|清}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Shun'ichi Toki]]<ref name="Kiyoshi"/>|Brandon Winckler<ref name="Kiyoshi">{{cite web|title=Kiyoshi Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Kiyoshi/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 4, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305003331/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Kiyoshi/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:Teruko and Shoichi's elder brother, who Kyogai kidnaps. He possesses a rare blood type known as 'marechi', making him a valued target to demons, who believe eating one marechi gives the same nutritional value as eating one hundred humans at once. 
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Hisa}}|ひさ}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Ikuko Tani]]|[[Barbara Goodson]]<ref>{{cite web|title=Hisa Voice – Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba (TV Show)|url=https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Hisa/|website=Behind the Voice Actors|access-date=March 5, 2023|archive-date=March 5, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230305000221/https://www.behindthevoiceactors.com/tv-shows/Demon-Slayer-Kimetsu-no-Yaiba/Hisa/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}
:An elderly woman who welcomes Demon Slayers to rest in her house, who Tanjiro and his group visit after fighting Kyogai.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Fuku}}|ふく}} {{nobold|and}} {{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Tomi}}|トミ}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Inori Minase]]|[[Anjali Kunapaneni]]}} (Fuku)
:{{Voiced by|[[Kikuko Inoue]]|[[Jill Remez]]}} (Tomi)
:A grandmother and granddaughter pair of bento sellers at a train station. They meet Kyojuro during his early investigation of the Mugen Train incident; he saves them from a demon that emerges from the train while it is being repaired. Years prior, Kyojuro's father, Shinjuro, saved Tomi and her daughter, Fuku's mother, from a demon, an incident which the former recalls after noticing the similarities between Kyojuro and Shinjuro's fighting styles. They only appear in the anime.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Keizo}}|慶蔵|Keizō}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Yuichi Nakamura]]|[[Channing Tatum]]}}
:Keizo was the master of Hakuji, who would go on become the demon Akaza. They met when he confronted Hakuji after beating several men in a fit of rage. Keizo defeated and made him his new student, teaching him the Soryu style. After making Hakuji his heir and allowing him to marry Koyuki, he was killed when a kendo dojo that wanted his land poisoned his drinking well. In his battle against Tanjiro and Giyu, Akaza sees Keizo's visage in Tanjiro because of his ideals, and after reliving his past and destroying his body, he reunited with Keizo's spirit, who encourages him despite his actions as a demon.
;{{Nihongo|{{vanchor|Koyuki}}|恋雪}}
:{{Voiced by|[[Lynn (voice actress)|Lynn]]|Rebecca Wang}}
:Koyuki was Keizo's daughter, who became Hakuji's fianceé. Born with a frail body, she grew up sick for most of her life. As a result, her mother committed suicide, and her father had given up on the possibility that she would ever heal. She met Hakuji after the latter was defeated by Keizo in combat, serving as her new caretaker. After she recovers, the two became engaged, until she was died after drinking from the dojo's well, which was laced to kill Keizo. During his battle in the Infinity Castle, Koyuki's spirit urged Hakuji to stop, pushing away Muzan's influence to help reconcile the demon with his lost humanity.

